add(151,'Three saving strategies','Financial and growth models','Ella and Omar each invest USD 18 000 toward a USD 32 000 target.',p('a','Ella earns 5.5% annually, compounded annually. Find her balance after 7 years to the nearest hundred dollars, and the first integer year when she reaches the target.',4,('M1',r'$V_7=18000(1.055)^7$.'),('A1',f'USD {round(18000*1.055**7,-2):,.0f}.'),('M1',r'$n\ge\ln(32000/18000)/\ln1.055$; round upward.'),('A1',f'$n={math.ceil(math.log(32000/18000)/math.log(1.055))}$.')),p('b','Omar earns r% nominal annually, compounded monthly. Rates are quoted to two decimal places. Find the minimum quoted rate that reaches the target in 10 years.',3,('M1',r'$18000(1+r/1200)^{120}\ge32000$.'),('A1',f'$r\\ge {rate:.6f}\\%$.'),('A1',f'The minimum quoted rate is {roundrate:.2f}%.')),p('c','Milo saves without interest. He makes an initial deposit P and, at each year-end, deposits one quarter of the preceding deposit. Show that P=18 000 can never reach the target. Find P that reaches it immediately after the seventh year-end deposit, to the nearest dollar.',7,('M1',r'Total deposits form $P+P/4+P/4^2+\cdots$.'),('A1',r'For P=18000 the infinite total is $18000/(1-1/4)=24000$.'),('R1',r'$24000<32000$, so that starting amount cannot reach the target.'),('R1','There are eight deposits including the initial one.'),('M1',r'$P(1-(1/4)^8)/(1-1/4)=32000$.'),('A1',r'$P=32000(3/4)/(1-(1/4)^8)$.'),('A1',f'USD {round(initial):,}.')))
