add(209,'A loan with a changing repayment plan','Financial and growth models','A loan of USD 360000 is repaid by 120 monthly payments of USD 4000, the first one month after borrowing. Interest is compounded monthly at nominal annual rate r%. Let k=1+r/1200.',p('a','Form an equation for k and find r.',6,('A1',r'After one payment the balance is $360000k-4000$.'),('M1','Iterate the balance recurrence to month 120.'),('A1',r'$0=360000k^{120}-4000(1+k+\cdots+k^{119})$.'),('A1',r'$90k^{120}=(k^{120}-1)/(k-1)$, with $k>1$.'),('M1','Solve the original annuity equation numerically; k=1 from a multiplied equation is extraneous.'),('A1',f'$k={kk:.8f}$, so $r={F(annual)}$%.')),p('b','Find the balance immediately after the 90th payment, to the nearest cent.',3,('M1',r'$B_{90}=360000k^{90}-4000(k^{90}-1)/(k-1)$.'),('A1','Substitute the unrounded interest multiplier.'),('A1',f'USD {D(bal)}.')),p('c','Alternatively the first 60 monthly payments are p dollars and the next 60 are 2p dollars. Find p, to the nearest cent.',8,('M1','Accumulate all payments to month 120.'),('A1',r'The first group contributes $pk^{60}(k^{60}-1)/(k-1)$.'),('A1',r'The second group contributes $2p(k^{60}-1)/(k-1)$.'),('M1','Equate their total to the accumulated initial loan.'),('A1',r'$360000k^{120}=p(k^{60}+2)(k^{60}-1)/(k-1)$.'),('A1',r'$p=360000k^{120}(k-1)/[(k^{60}+2)(k^{60}-1)]$.'),('M1','Use the unrounded k from (a).'),('A1',f'USD {D(pay)}.')))
